### Fix (test-only)

1. **`getDrawerWithProviderValue(expectedValue, { timeout })`** — Walks open `[data-testid="settings-drawer"][data-state="open"]:visible"` from newest to oldest, reads `settings-provider-select`’s `.value`, and returns the drawer that matches `expectedValue`, otherwise `drawers.last()`.

2. **`ensureConnectionPanel`** — Now supports `drawerSeed`; uses that drawer instead of always calling `getActiveSettingsDrawer()`. Activation uses scroll + tab click only (no `dismissBlockingOverlays`). Panel and `settings-connection-controls` visibility still use `visibilityTimeout` (defaults to 60s).

3. **Post–OpenRouter flow** — After `offline-kill-compact-after-openrouter-select.json`, the test attaches **`offline-kill-compact-before-ensure-panel.json`**, calls `getDrawerWithProviderValue('openrouter', { timeout: PHASE_MS })`, runs `ensureConnectionPanel({ drawerSeed, visibilityTimeout: PHASE_MS })` inside `withCompactOfflineKillDiagnostics('ensure-panel-failed', ...)`, then asserts OpenRouter on **`controlsAfterProvider`** with `provider-after-ensure-openrouter-failed`, then **`offline-kill-compact-after-ensure-panel.json`**.

